The graph of $|x+y|=10\sqrt{2}$ is a square with vertices at $(\pm 10\sqrt{2},0)$ and $(0,\pm 10\sqrt{2})$.  The graph of $x^{2}+y^{2}=100$ is a circle with radius $10$.  The points of intersection are $(\pm 5\sqrt{2},\pm 5\sqrt{2})$.  Therefore,
\[\left|x_{1}\right|+\left|y_{1}\right|+\left|x_{2}\right|+\left|y_{2}\right| = 5\sqrt{2}+5\sqrt{2}+5\sqrt{2}+5\sqrt{2} = \boxed{20\sqrt{2}}.\]
