Alternatively, Dennis and Edward can mow a lawn together in 24 minutes, the same amount of time it takes Shawn to mow a lawn. Since Shawn is mowing at the same rate as Dennis and Edward combined, Shawn, Dennis, and Edward together can mow 3 lawns in 24 minutes. Thus, in 2 hours, they can mow $3\cdot\frac{2\cdot 60}{24}=10$ lawns.

